--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
=== PARITY === (all 3 web hooks ported — web/src/api/hooks/useSettingsBackup.ts)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Reads / queries (0): none — the web domain has NO useQuery. All three hooks are
  useMutation (the user explicitly clicks Export / Preview / Apply; there is no polling
  case), so there is no Resource cache-then-network feed in this slice.

Mutations / actions (3):
  [x] useExportSettings -> SettingsBackupStore.exportSettings()
                           GET /settings/export ; decodes SettingsBundle.
                           onSuccess primes StateFlow lastExport = web
                           setQueryData(settingsBackupKeys.lastExport, bundle).
                           Verified by exportSettingsGetsSettingsExportAndDecodesBundle
                           + exportDelegatesAndCachesLastExport.
  [x] useDryRunImport   -> SettingsBackupStore.dryRunImport(bundle)
                           POST /settings/import ; body = { dry_run: true, bundle }
                           (bundle nested verbatim; opaque sections round-trip;
                           absent/null sections dropped = JSON.stringify / explicitNulls=false).
                           onSuccess primes StateFlow lastImport = web
                           setQueryData(settingsBackupKeys.lastImport, result).
                           Verified by dryRunImportPostsSettingsImportWithDryRunTrueAndBundle
                           + importBundleRoundTripsOpaqueSectionsAndDropsAbsentOnes
                           + dryRunDelegatesAndCachesLastImport.
  [x] useApplyImport    -> SettingsBackupStore.applyImport(bundle)
                           POST /settings/import ; body = { dry_run: false, bundle }.
                           onSuccess primes the SAME StateFlow lastImport (both web hooks
                           write settingsBackupKeys.lastImport). SUDO step-up is handled
                           transparently by the shared ApiHttpClient (web: the request()
                           client's SUDO_REQUIRED interceptor) — no bespoke plumbing.
                           Verified by applyImportPostsSettingsImportWithDryRunFalse
                           + applyDelegatesAndCachesLastImport
                           + applyAfterDryRunOverwritesLastImport.

Caching intent: the web hooks do NOT invalidateQueries; they setQueryData on the two flat
  keys settingsBackupKeys.lastExport / .lastImport. Reproduced as observable StateFlow
  state on the store (lastExport: StateFlow<SettingsBundle?>, lastImport:
  StateFlow<SettingsImportResult?>), updated only on mutation SUCCESS — proven by
  failedMutationsDoNotPrimeCache + lastResultStateStartsNull. Cache-key strings mirrored
  for C# parity (SETTINGS_BACKUP_PREFIX / settingsLastExportKey / settingsLastImportKey).

Derivations ported (with golden vectors, KMP+C# parity per ADR-004):
  [x] defaultExportFilename(epochMillis) = web defaultExportFilename
      "teslasync-settings-YYYYMMDD.json", UTC, month/day zero-padded, hour omitted.
      Golden: epoch_zero, two_digit_padding, year_rollover_eve, year_rollover_day,
      leap_day, fixed_now.
  [x] summariseImportResult(result) = web summariseImportResult
      total = added + updated (skipped summed separately, NOT in total).
      Golden: empty, single_section, multi_section, skipped_excluded_from_total.

Not ported (browser-only side effect, not portable): downloadSettingsBundle — uses Blob /
  document / URL.createObjectURL; the platform programs (P2/P3/P4) own the save-as action,
  driven by SettingsBackupStore.defaultExportFilename() + the exported bundle.

SI: no bundle/result field is unit-bearing (schema_version, RFC3339 exported_at, opaque
    JSON section payloads, integer add/update/skip counts, status text). Payloads
    round-trip verbatim — no SI conversion at this layer; display formatting is S5's job.

